  {
   "id": "R42-base-0006",
   "text": "After each impact test made in accordance with the conditions and procedure specified in Annex 3, the vehicle's propulsion, suspension (including tyres), steering and braking systems shall remain in adjustment and shall operate in a normal manner (where the EV charging inlet/flap is present in the bumper, this includes the propulsion/energy-supply parts in the impact zone); this requirement does not apply to sensors, cameras, radar devices, etc. being part of driver assist systems (e.g. the bumper's camera, radar, radar/LIDAR and PDC sensors), which may become damaged, disoriented or broken due to an impact carried out according to Annex 3 as long as the basic braking and steering performance are still intact.",
   "table": null,
   "regulation": "UN R42",
